  "text": "]={\nред ,\n\nocê insist}\n\n总而言欲###\n\nELCOME TO WIKIVISON  - the public wiki for wisdoms  .  Click on the detail link for more\n\n以下是数学问题的详细解答步骤：\n\nGiven the expression: $$\\frac{z}{z + 1} + \\frac{z}{z - 1} + \\frac{1}{z}$$\n\nFirst, find the common denominator for the first two terms:\n\nLCD: $(z + 1)(z - 1)$ due to difference of squares: $$(z - 1)(z + 1)$$\n\nConvert the first two terms:\n\n$$\\frac{z \\cdot (z - 1)}{(z + 1)(z - 1)} + \\frac{(z + 1)}{(z - 1)(z + 1)}$$\n\nSimplify:\n\n$$\\frac{z^2 - z + z + 1}{(z + 1)(z - 1)}$$\n\n$$\\frac{z^2 + 1}{(z + 1)(z - 1)}$$\n\nNow, let's add $\\frac{1}{z}$ to the above result:\n\n$$\\frac{z^2 + 1}{(z + 1)(z - 1)} + \\frac{1}{z}$$\n\nFind the common denominator:\n\n$$\\frac{(z^2 + 1)}{z(z + 1)(z - 1)} + \\frac{(z + 1)(z - 1)}{z(z + 1)(z - 1)}$$\n\nSimplify:\n\n$$\\frac{(z^2 + 1) + (z^2 - 1)}{z(z + 1)(z - 1)}$$\n\n$$\\frac{2z^2}{z(z^2 - 1)}$$\n\nCancel out $z$:\n\n$$\\frac{2z}{2^2(z - 1)(z + 1)}$$\n\nCancel out $z$:\n\n$$\\frac{2}{2(z - 1)(z + 1)}$$\n\nSimplify:\n\n$$\\frac{2}{2(z - 1)(z + 1)} -> \\frac{1}{(z - 1)(z + 1)}$$\n\nNow, we have a real expression.\n\nTo have this expression real, $(z - 1)(z + 1)$ must be purely imaginary or zero.\n\nTherefore, $$(z - 1)(z + 1) = 0$$\n\nWhich implies:\n\n$$z = 1$$ or $$z = -1$$\n\nSo the complex numbers that make the expression real are:\n\n\\boxed{1, -1}\n\n恭喜你找到了所有的解决方案！谢谢你的机会来检查这个问题。你是欢迎万维知识在翅膀[miranda](\tlogin)来进行你想要做的一切以检查这些问题。",
